al-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026.html#cor:gaussian","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:73585e3ba2bbd6edca1acbfc5b29990ca8b1e9ee9dffbb843a89e4a530c3e0df","file":"preprints/Stable-Self-Similar-Blowup-for-a-Supercritical-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026/build/main.tex","line":93,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5cf3dbe7121286d015629accdd53d4afa7cf337f49da08eec197c81b79c43fe2","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Stable-Self-Similar-Blowup-for-a-Supercritical-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:73585e3ba2bbd6edca1acbfc5b29990ca8b1e9ee9dffbb843a89e4a530c3e0df","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Stable-Self-Similar-Blowup-for-a-Supercritical-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026/build/main.tex#L93"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:gaussian}\nFor the fixed power $p$ and index $k$ in Theorem~\\ref{thm:blowup}, and\nfor every $\\alpha>k+6$, the initial datum\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:gaussian}\n u_0^\\omega(x)=\\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb Z^{12}}\n       g_n(\\omega)\\langle n\\rangle^{-\\alpha}e^{in\\cdot x}\n\\end{equation}\nbelongs to $H^k$ almost surely and has positive probability of finite-time\nblowup. In particular, the following assertion is false: for every\nenergy-supercritical pair $(d,p)$ there is a finite $\\alpha_0(d,p)$\nsuch that, for every $\\alpha>\\alpha_0(d,p)$ and every\n\\[\n d/2+2<m<\\alpha-d/2,\n\\]\nthe local $H^m$ solution with the Gaussian datum extends almost surely\nto $C(\\mathbb R;H^m(\\mathbb T^d))$."}
